{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790711560,"nonce":"bL3apzBiAOUxDm37iZQs0wOELVE=","title":"`zl_meta_of` calls `zl_file_metatable` for every dynamic metatable probe. Numeric `tostring` and `string.format` therefore make programs with no files adopt the file library, I/O adapters, and dynamic call machinery.","message":"On any_field this keeps 264 functions and adopts 255 imported bodies after the string-metatable fix. Reading the already-installed `zl_file_meta` instead reduces that to 193 kept functions and 184 adopted bodies. An actual file installs this metatable when it is created.\n\nMeasured with LLVM enabled over 21 interleaved runs:\n- Mac wall: 29.255 ms -\u003e 27.090 ms (7.4%)\n- x86_64 NUC wall: 34.652 ms -\u003e 31.956 ms (7.8%)\n- NUC LuaJIT wall: 2.203 ms\n\nAll variants produce result 1500000. The complete handwritten conformance suite passes in normal and warm-up modes, including metatables, stdlib, files and GC.","files":null}]}